00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:25.139
The model incorporates updated assumptions on robotaxi utilization rates and optimist deployment volumes.

00:06:25.559 --> 00:06:30.919
The file is available for public download and includes sensitivity tables for key input variables.

00:06:31.884 --> 00:06:38.584
Complex hand mechanisms continue to slow assembly timelines for the third generation optimist, global sources reports.

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:43.684
Workforce resistance at supplier sites has added further delays to scaling plans.

00:06:44.284 --> 00:06:48.224
Hand complexity exceeds initial engineering estimates by a significant margin.

00:06:48.224 --> 00:06:54.084
Supplier pushback centers on required precision tooling investments that have not yet been fully funded.

00:06:54.604 --> 00:07:00.684
Production of the third-generation robot remains gated by both the intricate finger assemblies and that labor resistance.

00:07:01.785 --> 00:07:09.265
Liner Truck 3 already moves more than 22,000 pounds, confirming the hardware's load capacity before the freight bed was added.

00:07:09.745 --> 00:07:16.905
A truck that tops out at 12 miles per hour and runs on 28 miles of range can operate inside a controlled flat route.

00:07:16.905 --> 00:07:22.365
In that tunnel, energy density and fast charging matter less than durability and simplicity.

00:07:22.885 --> 00:07:27.425
The trade-off is that the same hardware cannot easily migrate to higher speed or longer

00:07:27.425 --> 00:07:29.825
range surface applications without redesign.

00:07:30.365 --> 00:07:34.365
So the shared-part strategy works only inside a narrow operating window.

00:07:34.865 --> 00:07:39.945
Remote piloting from the Texas Operations Center removes the need for onboard driver interfaces

00:07:39.945 --> 00:07:44.385
or cabin safety systems that would add weight and cost on an open-road vehicle.

00:07:44.385 --> 00:07:49.865
Re-purposing automotive packs and drive units for underground freight changes the cost equation

00:07:49.865 --> 00:07:52.425
for both the vehicle maker and the tunneling company.

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:57.385
The components now handle freight without a new powertrain design, cutting the marginal

00:07:57.385 --> 00:07:59.065
expense of each additional truck.

00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:04.965
That reuse also reduces the number of unique parts the supply chain must support, which matters

00:08:04.965 --> 00:08:08.045
when production volumes for the base vehicle remain the priority.

00:08:08.685 --> 00:08:13.405
Over repeated cycles, the shared hardware can lower the per-unit cost of every liner truck

00:08:13.405 --> 00:08:15.465
that rolls out of the same supplier base.

00:08:16.005 --> 00:08:20.405
For Tesla, the arrangement creates a small but steady internal demand signal for cells

00:08:20.405 --> 00:08:23.565
and motors that would otherwise sit in finished vehicle inventory.

00:08:24.245 --> 00:08:29.265
Over time, those steady, low variability orders can help smooth factory utilization, even

00:08:29.265 --> 00:08:31.185
if external vehicle sales fluctuate.

00:08:31.685 --> 00:08:36.045
The current modification is an incremental step rather than a complete re-architecture.

00:08:36.565 --> 00:08:41.005
Whether the freight version finds paying external customers will determine if the reuse model

00:08:41.005 --> 00:08:44.605
becomes a repeatable margin lever or remains a niche demonstration.

00:08:45.145 --> 00:08:49.445
The valuation from September's funding round provides the runway to test that question

00:08:49.445 --> 00:08:50.505
at commercial volumes.

